A simple alternative to a global search is to partition the search interval into smaller
subintervals and apply the golden section method (or some other minimization algorithm)
to each of the subinterval. Of course, the success of this approach will depend on the
partition and could fail if some of the subintervals contain more than one local minimum.
Another similar, but distinctly di ff erent, option is to search using random subintervals. Two
numbers u 1, u 2 are generated from the uniform distribution over the search interval [a, b]
and a golden section search is conducted over the interval [min(u 1, u 2), max(u 1, u 2)]. The
process is repeated until some stopping criterion is met. This is the approach that will be
considered here.
